Why: The mixed-precision routines DMUMPS_LRMIXED_CAST, _PLUS and _GEMM
 (dlr_core.F, new in 5.9) take matrices of any precision through INTEGER
 dummies and only pass them on to the conversion/BLAS kernels; every call
 with REAL or DOUBLE PRECISION data is an argument mismatch, rejected by
 gfortran >= 10. Their dummies are now exempt from type, kind and rank
 checking (!GCC$ / !DEC$ ATTRIBUTES NO_ARG_CHECK, and !DIR$ IGNORE_TKR
 (TKRC) in the interfaces only: LLVM flang rejects IGNORE_TKR in the
 definition of an external procedure), which requires passing A and B
 rather than A(1) and B(1) on (same
 address) and explicit, equally type-agnostic interfaces for the kernels
 of lr_common.F they call (new mumps_lrmixed_kernels.h). Every caller
 needs explicit interfaces of the dispatch routines (new
 dmumps_lrmixed_interfaces.h): DMUMPS_LR_CORE provides them to its users
 (dsol_lr.F included), the external routines of dlr_core.F and
 DMUMPS_BLR_SAVE_DIAG_BLOCK include them. dsol_lr.F passes PT_RHS(1)
 instead of the whole
 rank-1 PT_RHS in the calls to the LRxFR/FRxFR routines that elsewhere
 receive an element (same storage, lower bound 1).
Upstream: not sent; worth offering with the MPI interfaces (0003).
Obsolete when: upstream declares these buffers type-agnostic.

